.SH NAME
<\f[I]name\f[R]> is matched by display name or description with precedence: exact, regex, fuzzy
.PP
You can identify them via logs e.g.
.IP
.EX
DP\-3 Arrived:
    name:     \(aqDP\-3\(aq
    desc:     \(aqUnknown Monitor Maker ABC123 (DP\-3 via HDMI)\(aq
.EE
.PP
It is recommended to use the description rather than the nondeterministic name.
.PP
Any item prefixed with a \f[B]\f[CB]!\f[B]\f[R] will be interpreted as extended POSIX regex e.g.\ \f[B]\f[CB]\(aq!\(haDP\-1\(aq\f[B]\f[R].
Regex strings must be single quoted.
.PP
Using a regex is preferred, however fuzzy case insensitive string matches of at least 4 characters may be used.
.PP
\f[CR]\(aqDP\-1\(aq\f[R] will match \f[CR]eDP\-1\f[R] and \f[CR]DP\-1\f[R].
Consider using regex \f[CR]\(aq!\(haDP\-1$\(aq\f[R] to exactly match.
.SH EXAMPLES
Add to your sway config to start way\-displays when sway starts:
.IP
.EX
exec way\-displays > /tmp/way\-displays.\(rs${XDG_VTNR}.\(rs${USER}.log 2>&1
.EE
.PP
Show current configuration and display state:
.IP
.EX
way\-displays \-g
.EE
.PP
List the connected displays:
.IP
.EX
way\-displays \-l
.EE
.PP
Arrange left to right, aligned at the bottom:
.IP
.EX
way\-displays \-s ARRANGE_ALIGN row bottom
.EE
.PP
Set the order for arrangement:
.IP
.EX
way\-displays \-s ORDER \(rs\(dq!\(haDP\-[0\-9]+$\(rs\(dq HDMI\-1 \(rs\(dqmonitor maker ABC model XYZ\(rs\(dq eDP\-1
.EE
.PP
Set the scale:
.IP
.EX
way\-displays \-s SCALE \(rs\(dqeDP\-1\(rs\(dq 3
.EE
.PP
Use 3840x2160\(at24Hz for HDMI\-A\-1:
.IP
.EX
way\-displays \-s MODE HDMI\-A\-1 3840 2160 24
.EE
.PP
Persist your changes to your \f[B]\f[CB]cfg.yaml\f[B]\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
way\-displays \-w
.EE
